content:
eli: Quick repro: SDK helper does call.execute() catch IOException -> call.clone().execute(), which can send duplicate POSTs when a coroutine cancels mid-flight. Seen on emulator with network delay.

maria: can you share minimal snippet?

eli: sure:
```kotlin
suspend fun safeExecute(call: Call): Response = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
  try { call.execute() } catch (e: IOException) { call.clone().execute() }
}
```

devin: clone() is the culprit. If the original call was cancelled by coroutine cancellation the clone will happily run and send a second POST.

qa-mika: frequency? any customer hits?

eli: low but real; one customer reported duplicate orders. Repro on emulator with `adb shell network delay` by cancelling scope after 1s. ~20% dupes in quick runs.

maria: short-term: stop automatic retries for non-idempotent methods unless caller sets "Idempotency-Key". Also add telemetry when a retry would occur.

devin: long-term: replace execute() helper with cancellable wrapper using enqueue + suspendCancellableCoroutine so cancellation cancels the active call:```kotlin
suspend fun Call.awaitResponse(): Response = suspendCancellableCoroutine { cont ->
  enqueue(object: Callback {
    override fun onResponse(c: Call, r: Response) { if (!cont.isCancelled) cont.resume(r) }
    override fun onFailure(c: Call, e: IOException) { if (!cont.isCancelled) cont.resumeWithException(e) }
  })
  cont.invokeOnCancellation { cancel() }
}
```

qa-mika: can we add a CI emulator stress test that shapes network and cancels coroutines to assert single POST?

maria: yes—I'll add a 1000-iteration emulator job and push a PR that: 1) removes naive clone retry, 2) adds idempotency guard + telemetry, 3) introduces cancellable wrapper, 4) documents migration notes for customers using auth-in-interceptor.

build-bot: created SDK ticket SDK-5001 and queued emulator job (run #1).

eli: thanks team. I'll include a tiny sample app in the PR so reviewers can run the repro locally. :thumbsup:
